## Using Creative Commons Public Licenses

Creative Commons public licenses provide a standard set of terms and conditions that creators and other rights holders can use to share original works of authorship and other material subject to copyright and certain other rights specified in the public license below. The following considerations are for informational purposes only, are not exhaustive, and do not form part of our licenses.

* **Considerations for licensors:** Our public licenses are intended for use by licensors to authorize others to exercise certain limited rights not reserved by copyright. By exercising any rights granted, licensors acknowledge and agree to be bound by the terms and conditions of this license. If you do not want to grant others the right to use your material under the terms of this license, consider licensing under different terms.

* **Considerations for the public:** By exercising any rights granted, users acknowledge and agree to be bound by the terms and conditions of this license. The licensor grants the rights under this license only to the extent they legally can, so the license does not apply where the exercise of any rights exceeds that scope. The exercise of rights granted by this license is subject to the same limitations as copyright, so the license does not excuse you from compliance with any non-copyright legal requirements (such as defamation, right of publicity, and contractual obligations).

* **Attribution:** In addition to the conditions in this license, you must include a credit to the original author in a reasonable manner. You may satisfy this condition by including a reference to the original work and indicating if any modifications were made.

* **NonCommercial:** You may not use the material for commercial purposes. Commercial purposes means use of the work in connection with any activity that generates revenue, profit, or other compensation.

* **No Derivatives:** You may not alter, transform, or build upon the work. You may not create derivative works. If you mix or modify the work in a way that would make a derivative work, you may not distribute it.

